/ locals: current_server, target_uid, spec
/ One admin player-action control, in its own region so a settled response can replace just this one. A balance action is
/ an amount field with Give/Remove; a character action is a single button that stretches to fill the column height (kill
/ confirms). Each carries a fresh idempotency key, so a double-click dedupes and the region re-renders with a new key
/ after it fires. The action is sent as player_action, not action - `action` is Rails' reserved routing key.
- if player_balance_action?(spec[:action])
  div id=player_action_region_id(spec[:action])
    = form_with url: modify_server_player_path(current_server.public_id, target_uid), method: :post do |form|
      = form.hidden_field :player_action, value: spec[:action]
      = form.hidden_field :idempotency_key, value: SecureRandom.uuid
      .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2
        span.fw-medium.text-nowrap.flex-shrink-0 style="width: 5.5rem"
          i class="bi bi-#{spec[:icon]} me-1 text-secondary-emphasis"
          = spec[:label]
        = form.number_field :amount, class: "form-control flex-grow-1", placeholder: "Amount", min: 1, required: true
        = form.button "Give", type: "submit", name: "direction", value: "give", class: "btn btn-outline-success flex-shrink-0"
        = form.button "Remove", type: "submit", name: "direction", value: "remove", class: "btn btn-outline-danger flex-shrink-0"
- else
  div id=player_action_region_id(spec[:action])
    = button_to modify_server_player_path(current_server.public_id, target_uid),
      params: {player_action: spec[:action], idempotency_key: SecureRandom.uuid},
      class: "btn btn-#{spec[:variant]} w-100 d-flex flex-column align-items-center justify-content-center gap-1",
      form: {data: {turbo_confirm: spec[:confirm]}} do
      i class="bi bi-#{spec[:icon]} fs-4"
      span.fw-medium = spec[:label]
